Documentation programs
======================

The .cpp files in this directory exist to be QUOTED BY THE GENEVA MANUAL: where
the real library code is too heavyweight to excerpt honestly, the manual shows a
small, complete program instead (rule D2 in the manual repository's
DOCUMENTATION-INVARIANTS.md). Every program here

  * compiles and links against this library's own dependency closure only,
  * runs as an S-size ctest case, so it cannot rot without turning a gate red,
  * carries //! [anchor] snippet markers that the manual's extraction layer
    reads (see source/snippets.map in the manual repository).

They are deliberately separate from examples/: an example teaches a user how to
use the library, a documentation program backs a specific listing in the manual.
Treat marker pairs like code -- moving or deleting one breaks the manual build,
which names the affected chapter.
